WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.023
Crawling is the process of discovering reachable pages, endpoints, routes, forms, links, parameters, and API surfaces.

2
00:00:08.023 --> 00:00:12.307
Traditional web pages may be discovered through links and forms.

3
00:00:12.307 --> 00:00:18.382
Single-page applications may require browser execution and client-side route awareness.

4
00:00:18.382 --> 00:00:23.523
APIs may require documentation, schemas, collections, or example requests.

5
00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:28.664
Mobile backends may expose routes that are not obvious from a desktop browser.

6
00:00:28.664 --> 00:00:31.624
Coverage determines what DAST can evaluate.

7
00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:41.828
If the scanner cannot reach an endpoint, authenticate into a workflow, discover a route, or understand a request format, it cannot reliably test that area.

8
00:00:41.828 --> 00:00:51.798
Authenticated pages, role-specific functionality, hidden routes, tenant-specific views, and stateful workflows often require additional setup.

9
00:00:51.798 --> 00:01:00.599
OpenAPI or API descriptions at a high level can help scanners understand API shape, but they still need valid context and credentials.

10
00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:02.858
Session state affects discovery.

11
00:01:02.858 --> 00:01:13.997
Some workflows require creating a record before editing it, adding an item before checking out, or moving through a sequence before a later endpoint becomes meaningful.

12
00:01:13.997 --> 00:01:20.384
A scanner that sends requests out of order may miss important behavior or produce noisy findings.

13
00:01:20.384 --> 00:01:27.238
Test data and repeatable setup steps help DAST cover realistic paths without damaging production data.

14
00:01:27.238 --> 00:01:30.120
Coverage gaps should be reported honestly.

15
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:36.118
A clean scan of the public landing page does not mean the authenticated application is safe.

16
00:01:36.118 --> 00:01:41.726
A scan that excludes administrative features cannot speak for administrative risk.

17
00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:50.216
Strong DAST programs track what was in scope, what was reached, what was excluded, and which areas require other testing methods.

18
00:01:50.216 --> 00:01:54.266
Coverage transparency keeps results useful and defensible.
